 "notes": "Hand-transcribed from a faxed score sheet (page 1 boys, page 2 girls; Central Middle School, teams Central, Sedomocha, Airline, Ridge View, All Saints; 9/20/18), every row read twice. The fax prints only the first time of a run of the same minute, so later times carry the minute of the line above (':38' after 11:00 is 11:38); every time was filled that way and checked to rise with place. Distance is not printed: set to 1.9 Mile Run CC because the other 2018 meets with these same teams (the 9/27 meet and the 10/18 Inland championship) are 1.9 miles; this is an inference. Codes: R = Ridge View School, AS = All Saints, C = Central Middle School, A = Airline, S = Sedomocha (the sheet writes Sedo). Boys: an arrow beside Willis Rienhardt/Mike Connolly (places 10, 11) is kept in the printed order, times rise. Girls: Elise Ouellette (15) has an inked-over time that cannot be read, stored NT (between 15:05 and 15:26 by neighbours); Ceseria 15:26 and Kiera Whitehouse 16:14 had their first digit blotted and were read from neighbours; surnames Pitma (Annajane), Roncoe and Lazon-Babet are the visible letters. Team scores: boys Ridge View 22 (2+3+4+5+8) reproduces; Airline 28 = 13+15 and Sedomocha 69 = 16+22+31 are the sums of all their (2 and 3) runners; All Saints is printed 103 (then a second figure 104 under it) and equals the sum of ALL SIX of its runners 1+6+7+27+28+34, whereas the usual top five would be 69, so the sheet scored it on six; Central (5th) has no total printed (its top five would be 89, which does not sit behind All Saints 103 either). Girls: Ridge View 18 (1+2+3+5+7) and Central 133 (18+24+26+32+33) reproduce; All Saints 64 does NOT reproduce from any reading (top five by place 6+8+10+11+12 = 47, six runners 62, seven 81) and is left out of team_rankings (so the verifier checks only Ridge View and Central there); Central boys is also left out (no total printed); 4th place left blank on the sheet."
